.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.\" Title
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.TH omc 1 "" "OpenModelica @OM_MANPAGE_VERSION@" "OpenModelica User Commands"
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH NAME
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
omc \- OpenModelica Compiler \- A Modelica compiler / interpreter based on free
software
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.B omc
.RI [ options ]
.RI ( Model.mo " | " Script.mos )
.RI [ libraries " | " .mo\-files ]
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.B omc
is the OpenModelica compiler. Given a Modelica file
.RI ( .mo )
it prints the flattened model on standard output, or, with
.BR \-s ,
generates simulation code for it. Given a script
.RI ( .mos )
it runs the scripting commands in it, which can load, translate, simulate and
plot models. The scripting API is documented in the built\-in package
.B OpenModelica.Scripting
and in the OpenModelica User's Guide at
<https://openmodelica.org/doc/OpenModelicaUsersGuide/@OM_MANPAGE_DOC_VERSION@/scripting_api.html>.
.PP
.I libraries
are fully qualified names of libraries, such as
.BR Modelica ,
to load before the model or script is processed.
.PP
Generated code, simulation executables and result files are written to the
current working directory.
.PP
The clients shipped with OpenModelica, such as
.BR OMEdit (1),
.BR OMShell (1)
and
.BR OMNotebook (1),
link the compiler in and do not start
.BR omc .
With
.B \-\-interactive
it runs as a server for tools in other processes, such as OMPython.
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH OPTIONS
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
An option's value is given as
.BI \-\- flag = value
or
.BI \-\- flag " value"\c
, and likewise for the short forms. Only the most common ones are listed here;
.B omc \-\-help
lists all of them.
.
.SS "General"
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help [ =\fItopic\fP ]
Display the help text. The topics are
.B omc
(the compiler options),
.B debug
(the debug flags),
.B optmodules
(the symbolic optimisation modules),
.B simulation
(the options of generated simulation executables) and
.I flagname
for the description of a single flag;
.B \-\-help=topics
lists them.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-silent
Turn on silent mode.
.TP
.BI \-d ", " \-\-debug= flags
Set debug flags, separated by commas. See
.BR \-\-help=debug .
.TP
.BI \-\-cmd= script
Execute the string argument as a script before any other operation.
.TP
.BI \-n ", " \-\-numProcs= n
The number of processors to use; 0, the default, chooses automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-locale= locale
Override the locale from the environment.
.TP
.BI \-r ", " \-\-alarm= seconds
Time out after
.IR seconds .
The running command is first asked to stop; omc exits outright a tenth of
that time later if it does not.
.
.SS "Language"
.TP
.BI \-g ", " \-\-grammar= grammar
The grammar and semantics to accept:
.B Modelica
(the default),
.BR MetaModelica ,
.BR ParModelica ,
.B Optimica
or
.BR PDEModelica .
.TP
.BI \-\-std= version
The Modelica language standard:
.BR 1.x ,
.BR 2.x ,
.B 3.0
to
.BR 3.6 ,
.B latest
(the default) or
.BR experimental .
.TP
.BI \-\-annotationVersion= version
The annotation version:
.BR 1.x ,
.B 2.x
or
.B 3.x
(the default).
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Enforce the Modelica language rules more strictly.
.TP
.B \-\-showErrorMessages
Show error messages immediately when they happen.
.TP
.B \-\-showAnnotations
Show annotations in the flattened code.
.TP
.B \-\-noSimplify
Do not simplify expressions.
.
.SS "Translation and simulation"
.TP
.BI \-i ", " \-\-instClass= class
Instantiate the class given by its fully qualified name.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-simulationCg
Generate simulation code.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-simulation
Simulate the last model in the given Modelica file.
.TP
.BI \-\-simCodeTarget= target
The target language of the generated code, such as
.B C
(the default) or
.BR Cpp .
.TP
.BI \-\-target= compiler
The compiler the generated code is built with, such as
.BR gcc .
.TP
.BR \-\-linkType= \fIdynamic\fP | \fIstatic\fP
Link the simulation executable against shared libraries (fast to build, not
portable) or static ones.
.TP
.BI \-\-cppFlags= flags
Extra flags for compiling with the C++ compiler, for example
.BR \-\-cppFlags=\-O3,\-Wall .
.TP
.B \-\-daeMode
Generate code that passes the whole system to the DAE solver IDA.
.
.SS "FMU export"
.TP
.B \-\-export\-fmu
Export the model as an FMU after loading it.
.TP
.BI \-\-fmiVersion= version
The FMI version:
.BR 1.0 ,
.B 2.0
or
.BR 3.0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-fmuType= type
The FMU type:
.BR me ,
.BR cs ,
.B me_cs
or
.BR se .
.TP
.BI \-\-fmuPlatforms= platforms
The platforms to build the FMU for, separated by commas, for example
.BR static,dynamic .
.
.SS "Server"
.TP
.BI \-\-interactive= mode
Run as a server:
.B none
(the default),
.B tcp
or
.BR zmq .
The TCP server listens on port 29500. The ZeroMQ server writes the port it
listens on to
.RI $TMPDIR/openmodelica. user .port suffix .
.TP
.BI \-\-interactivePort= port
The port of the ZeroMQ server; 0, the default, picks a free one.
.TP
.BI \-z ", " \-\-zeroMQFileSuffix= suffix
The suffix of the ZeroMQ port file.
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.TP
.B OPENMODELICAHOME
The installation directory. By default it is derived from the location of the
.B omc
executable.
.TP
.B OPENMODELICALIBRARY
The Modelica library path. The default is
.IR ~/.openmodelica/libraries/ ,
where the package manager installs libraries. When it is empty,
.B omc
fills it with the libraries shipped in the installation's
.IR share/omlibrary/cache/ .
.TP
.B TMPDIR
The temporary directory. The default is
.IR /tmp .
.TP
.B MODELICAUSERCFLAGS
Extra flags for the C compiler when building a simulation executable.
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH EXAMPLES
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.TP
.B omc Model.mo
Print the flattened model on standard output.
.TP
.B omc \-s Model.mo
Generate simulation code for the model:
.IR Model.c ,
.IR Model_functions.c ,
.I Model.makefile
and
.IR Model_init.xml .
.TP
.B omc Script.mos
Run the commands in
.IR Script.mos .
.TP
.B omc Model.mo Modelica
Load the Modelica Standard Library, then print the flattened model.
.TP
.B omc \-\-export\-fmu \-i MyModel \-\-fmiVersion=2.0 MyModel.mo Modelica
Load
.I MyModel.mo
and the Modelica Standard Library, then export
.B MyModel
as an FMU.
.PP
A script that simulates a model and plots two of its variables:
.PP
.RS
.nf
loadModel(Modelica);
loadFile("dcmotor.mo");
simulate(dcmotor, stopTime=10.0);
plot({load.w, load.phi});
.fi
.RE
.
